[
  {
    "sha": "1672130016b468b9bfaa5d61077af63249f952c2",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDE2NzIxMzAwMTZiNDY4YjliZmFhNWQ2MTA3N2FmNjMyNDlmOTUyYzI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-15T20:00:04Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-15T20:00:04Z"
      },
      "message": "test(ui): named page layout tests; behaviour tests without fixed positions\n\nPrepare the UI tests for the refit (#655), so that a refit PR updates\nsmall named tests and does not need hours of retest at the cut gate.\n\n- page_layout.rs: one coarse layout test for the shell (dark and light),\n  each property page and the Debug info window (15 tests). Each asserts\n  that the anchor widgets are inside the Properties leaf and stack top\n  to bottom, and names the page on failure.\n- structural::assert_shell_skeleton asserts presence, labels and the\n  enabled state only; its positions moved to assert_shell_layout.\n- anchors.rs: pane_center and chrome_point take pointer targets from\n  the live layout and replace fixed points (4,4), (1100,500),\n  (640,712) and the y > 600 status lookup.\n- AGENTS.md / crates/ui/AGENTS.md: the rule \"A UI refit PR keeps its\n  tests\".\n- docs/decisions/1953-ui-refit-test-plan.md.\n\nThe painted ribbon cells and browser rows have no AccessKit nodes yet;\nthe tests that reach them by geometry go to #1988 and #1989.\n\nRefs #1953\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
